#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_snare.name"
msgstr "Wire Snare"

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_snare.description"
msgstr "A loop of cord or wire set across a game trail, tightened by a springy branch. Cheap enough to deploy more than one, unreliable enough that materials still matter. The wire remembers the shape of the animal it was meant to hold."

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_deadfall.name"
msgstr "Deadfall Trap"

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_deadfall.description"
msgstr "A flat stone or salvaged plate balanced on a trigger stick. Low-tech, material-light, and as old as hunger. The trigger is the hard part. The rest is weight and patience."

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_pit.name"
msgstr "Pit Trap"

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_pit.description"
msgstr "A concealed pit dug into a game trail, lined with sharpened stakes. Labor-heavy, location-dependent, and capable of stopping something large. The earth does the work. The survivor does the digging."

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_net.name"
msgstr "Net Trap"

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_net.description"
msgstr "A mesh of cord or salvaged netting strung between posts or branches. Broader coverage than a snare, higher upfront cost, and more things can go wrong. Birds and small mammals both tangle in it."

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_fish.name"
msgstr "Fish Trap"

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_fish.description"
msgstr "A woven funnel of wood and cord set in moving water. Fish enter but cannot find the exit. Strong where geography supports it, worthless where it does not. The freeze kills it. The thaw brings it back."

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_cage.name"
msgstr "Cage Trap"

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_cage.description"
msgstr "A sprung cage of salvaged metal and wire, triggered by weight on a plate. Expensive to build, durable once built. The animal lives inside it, which is either a mercy or a problem depending on what caught."

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_bird_snare.name"
msgstr "Bird Snare"

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_bird_snare.description"
msgstr "A fine noose of thread or thin wire set on a perch stick. Lightweight, fast to deploy, and fragile. Frequent small calories with a health-risk shadow."

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_body_grip.name"
msgstr "Body-Grip Trap"

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_body_grip.description"
msgstr "A heavy spring-loaded mechanism that closes steel jaws on anything that passes through the frame. Efficient, durable, and severe. The misfire is as dangerous as the catch."

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_box.name"
msgstr "Box Trap"

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_box.description"
msgstr "A wooden box with a gravity door, triggered by a treadle inside. Bulky, dependable, and shelter-craftable. The animal is alive when you check it, which is the point."

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_improvised_wire.name"
msgstr "Improvised Wire Snare"

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.trap.trap_improvised_wire.description"
msgstr "A twist of copper wire shaped into a loose loop and pegged to the ground. The poorest survivor's option, better than doing nothing. It breaks often, catches little, and costs almost nothing to replace."

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.prey.rabbit.name"
msgstr "Ash Rabbit"

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.prey.rabbit.description"
msgstr "A small grey-brown rabbit, lean from foraging in contaminated soil. Common enough to teach the trapping loop, modest enough to keep the survivor humble."

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.prey.cotton_hare.name"
msgstr "Cotton Hare"

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.prey.cotton_hare.description"
msgstr "A larger hare with pale winter fur that darkens in the thaw. Faster and less common than the rabbit, with a slightly stronger yield."

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.prey.deer.name"
msgstr "Wasteland Mule Deer"

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
msgid "wildlife.prey.deer.description"
msgstr "A gaunt mule deer, ribs showing through a dusty coat. Rare jackpot, never baseline passive food."

#: Assets/StreamingAssets/Data/wildlife_trapping_catalog.json
